{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"As of 2026-09-22 several streams remain blocked while others are only reopened. What work can advance in parallel, what cannot progress until an external dependency moves, and what release checklist work is gated on packaging and Windows signing?"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nPre-release gate review: Docker slim/CVE, Windows signing, and upstream high-DPI remain open. Audit-log path still a hold — CLI schema and emitted records don't match.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-10\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Pre-Release Audit\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-15\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Alice**: We're in pre-release mode. Gate check first: Docker slim-down and CVE work is still open, Windows signing is still open, and we're still blocked upstream on the high-DPI rendering bug. Those stay on the board. Diana, where are we on the audit-log gate?\\n\\n**Diana**: Still a hold. The CLI path and the log records aren't matching the schema we defined. That undercuts the audit trail as release evidence.\\n\\n**Bob**: I've been wiring audit-log generation into the CLI. The shape coming out still isn't consistent with what the schema expects — I've got another pass queued.\\n\\n**Charlie**: So this isn't a packaging issue — it's schema versus emitted records?\\n\\n**Diana**: Yes. Until those match, I can't clear the audit gate.\\n\\n**Evan**: That stacks on top of the Docker and Windows holds Alice listed. Release isn't opening with any of those unresolved.\\n\\n**Alice**: Correct. Security-gate work stays open — Docker slim-down, Windows signing, and we keep the audit mismatch visible as a release blocker. No one closes those today.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep the audit-log gate red until schema and records match.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari pre releas gate review docker slim cve window sign and upstream high dpi remain open audit log path still a hold cli schema and emit record don t match sourc id src meet 10 firefli transcript pre releas audit date 2026 09 15 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript alic we re in pre releas mode gate check first docker slim down and cve work is still open window sign is still open and we re still block upstream on the high dpi render bug those stay on the board diana where are we on the audit log gate diana still a hold the cli path and the log record aren t match the schema we defin that undercut the audit trail a releas evid bob i ve been wire audit log generat into the cli the shape come out still isn t consist with what the schema expect i ve got anoth pas queu charli so this isn t a packag issu it s schema versus emit record diana yes until those match i can t clear the audit gate evan that stack on top of the docker and window hold alic list releas isn t open with ani of those unresolv alic correct secur gate work stay open docker slim down window sign and we keep the audit mismatch visibl a a releas blocker no one close those today diana i ll keep the audit log gate red until schema and record match\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"id\": \"be17298264309b61\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30576383513016275, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11161908161451825, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75876826, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94edcc88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-15-Pre-Release-Audit.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1495, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:06\", \"token_count\": 424, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-37\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Signing Gap\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 09:14] Evan**: Windows Defender and SmartScreen are both flagging the build for pilot testers — unsigned binaries get treated as untrusted by default.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:13] Alice**: Is the missing code-signing certificate the actual blocker here?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:14] Evan**: Yes. We still don't have one. Until we do, every pilot install is going to trip a warning at best, get blocked outright at worst.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:16] Diana**: Release blocker?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30157129481953415, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0942379925993345, \"vector_similarity\": 0.785349, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 927, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:53\", \"token_count\": 288, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28973563702512867, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0833040243216124, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7714094, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2883267553836669, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11169145054809562, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7004758, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n# Release Checklist — v1.0 Gate Status (Draft)\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2005\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-12\\n\\nDraft checklist for T011 (Release v1.0 Gates). Per the task's own dependency list, this draft depends on T001 through T006 and T010.\\n\\n## Gate Status as of Today\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n# Release Checklist — v1.0 Gate Status (Draft)\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2005\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-12\\n\\nDraft checklist for T011 (Release v1.0 Gates). Per the task's own dependency list, this draft depends on T001 through T006 and T010.\\n\\n## Blocking Item\\n\\nT005 is the only unmet dependency: the Docker image failed Diana's size/CVE review and was reopened on 2026-06-25. This checklist cannot close until that gate clears.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n# Release Checklist — v1.0 Gate Status (Draft)\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2005\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-07-12\\n\\nDraft checklist for T011 (Release v1.0 Gates). Per the task's own dependency list, this draft depends on T001 through T006 and T010.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nActive (Draft). Six of seven dependency gates are met; T005 remains open.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 05 releas checklist v1 0 gate status draft